{"text": "\u2018 XC: SENT TO DR. A. SPEARS & DR. F. SCHULTZ - 10/31/85.\nJAMES H. STARKEY, Il, Vice President JAMES M, DAIL, Treasurer\na HUGH C. KIGER, Executive Vice President\nyale J.T. BUNN, Executive Director OCT 50 ms\n17% LEAF TOBACCO EXPORTERS ASSOCIATION, INC. .\n\n\u201cFor the purpose of protecting and promoting the market\n\nEXECUTIVE COMMITTEE:\nT. WAYNE OAKES, Chairman\nAP. THORPE, i\nAMES H. STARKEY, I\nJAMES M. DAIL\nFOSTER LYNCH\nW. 7. ANDERSON\n\u2018ALLEN KING\nCLAUDE 8. OWEN, JA.\nPAY 5. LEWIS\n\u2018ALBERT MONK, ti\nHN. HARDY, JA\nKARL E ANDERSEN\nJOHN L_ HOWARD\nEDDIE FOY, JA.\n\n\u2018The Honorable Jesse Helm:\n\nfor American Leat Tobacco\u201d\n\nEXECUTIVE OFFICES\n3716 NATIONAL DRIVE, SUITE 114\nRALEIGH, NORTH CAROLINA 27612\nTelephone: (919) 7825151\n\n29 October 1985\n\nChairman, Senate Committee on\n\nAgriculture, Nutrition\n\n& Forestry\n\n328A Senate Russell Office Building\n\nWashington, D.C. 20510\n\nDear Jesse:\n\nWe congratulate you on the skillful manner in which you have moved S. 1418\nthrough the Senate. It would be good if the Bill is passed soon with a\n\n\u2018minimum of changes.\n\nA few days ago, Senator Albert Gore of Tenn\n\njee introduced an amendment\n\nto the Senate Farm Bill S. 1714 ~ relating to Tobacco Pesticide Reoidues.\nThe amendment provides for (1) a certification by the importer that\n\nimported tobacco has not\n\nbeen produced or processed with the use of a\n\nPesticide that is not registered under the FIFR Act, (2) the Secretary\nshall sample and test tobacco offered for importation on entry into the\nU.S. to determine whether that tobacco conforms with the certification\nFequired under this subsection, (3) domestically produced tobacco is\nSubject to substantially the same requirements with respect to residues\nof any pesticide as apply to tobacco offered for importation, and (4) if\nthe Secretary determines that flue-cured and Burley tobacco (from 1986\nand future crops which receive price supports) does not meet the require-\nments of this section, such tobacco may not be moved in commerce among the\nstates and shall be destroyed by the Secretary.\n\nThe members of the trade associations which I represent, Leaf Tobacco\nExporters Association and Tobacco Association of United States, purchase\nabout 70 percent of U.S. tobacco crops and export most all U.S. tobacco\nshipped overse:\n\nA list of the members of LTEA and TAUS is attached (Attachment A).\n\nS9ECTZLE", "words": [{"text": "\u2018", "x0": 18, "y0": 18, "x1": 29, "y1": 28, "conf": 45.0}, {"text": "XC:", "x0": 269, "y0": 27, "x1": 291, "y1": 36, "conf": 77.0}, {"text": "SENT", "x0": 312, "y0": 27, "x1": 344, "y1": 36, "conf": 86.0}, {"text": "TO", "x0": 354, "y0": 28, "x1": 370, "y1": 37, "conf": 93.0}, {"text": "DR.", "x0": 380, "y0": 28, "x1": 402, "y1": 37, "conf": 96.0}, {"text": "A.", "x0": 413, "y0": 28, "x1": 427, "y1": 37, "conf": 95.0}, {"text": "SPEARS", "x0": 440, "y0": 28, "x1": 489, "y1": 38, "conf": 93.0}, {"text": "&", "x0": 500, "y0": 30, "x1": 506, "y1": 38, "conf": 93.0}, {"text": "DR.", "x0": 517, "y0": 29, "x1": 539, "y1": 38, "conf": 92.0}, {"text": "F.", "x0": 551, "y0": 29, "x1": 565, "y1": 38, "conf": 91.0}, {"text": "SCHULTZ", "x0": 577, "y0": 29, "x1": 635, "y1": 39, "conf": 93.0}, {"text": "-", "x0": 645, "y0": 33, "x1": 652, "y1": 35, "conf": 92.0}, {"text": "10/31/85.", "x0": 663, "y0": 29, "x1": 736, "y1": 40, "conf": 92.0}, {"text": "JAMES", "x0": 330, "y0": 50, "x1": 363, "y1": 58, "conf": 91.0}, {"text": "H.", "x0": 367, "y0": 50, "x1": 376, "y1": 58, "conf": 59.0}, {"text": "STARKEY,", "x0": 380, "y0": 50, "x1": 427, "y1": 60, "conf": 95.0}, {"text": "Il,", "x0": 431, "y0": 51, "x1": 442, "y1": 60, "conf": 65.0}, {"text": "Vice", "x0": 445, "y0": 51, "x1": 465, "y1": 59, "conf": 65.0}, {"text": "President", "x0": 469, "y0": 52, "x1": 513, "y1": 60, "conf": 29.0}, {"text": "JAMES", "x0": 616, "y0": 55, "x1": 649, "y1": 64, "conf": 91.0}, {"text": "M,", "x0": 653, "y0": 56, "x1":